	<logo>https://static.globalissues.org/i/globalissues/logo-feed.jpg</logo><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/10/14/41326</id><title>Taliban’s New Internet Restrictions Keep Afghanistan Out of the Global Spotlight</title><updated>2025-10-14T16:24:27-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/10/14/41326" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2025/10/internetrestrictions2.jpg?v=1" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2025/10/internetrestrictions2.jpg?v=1&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;KABUL, October 14 (IPS)  - At the end of September, the Taliban abruptly severed Wi-Fi and fiber-optic internet in Afghanistan for 48 hours without any explanation. The disruption caused consternation and suffering among millions of Afghans, especially those who depend on the internet for education and online commerce.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/10/14/41326&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Taliban’s New Internet Restrictions Keep Afghanistan Out of the Global Spotlight”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2025/10/internetrestrictions2-100x100.jpg?v=1" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/10/14/41323</id><title>World Bank and Other MDBs Need to Tackle Rich Country GHG Emissions to Support Development</title><updated>2025-10-14T12:18:21-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/10/14/41323" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2025/10/Privatization_-629x419-1.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2025/10/Privatization_-629x419-1.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
WASHINGTON DC, October 14 (IPS)  - The World Bank and other multilateral development banks recently have begun &lt;a id=&quot;m_-94292403662109932OWA650a87e7-ec88-560c-280e-f1c22ba589cd&quot; href=&quot;https://www.tradingview.com/news/reuters.com,2025:newsml_L1N3QU0P7:0-world-bank-s-banga-seeks-board-approval-for-all-of-the-above-energy-strategy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.tradingview.com/news/reuters.com,2025:newsml_L1N3QU0P7:0-world-bank-s-banga-seeks-board-approval-for-all-of-the-above-energy-strategy/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1760529771440000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2vBY3BID4vXCag4KBdJBdO&quot;&gt;reconsidering their self-imposed restrictions on financing fossil fuel projects&lt;/a&gt;. This change is being prompted in part by &lt;a id=&quot;m_-94292403662109932OWAc0f00713-5ae8-4fa5-462b-2e4209b3a66b&quot; href=&quot;https://www.climatechangenews.com/2025/05/13/trump-shifts-us-energy-funding-from-shutting-down-foreign-fossil-fuels-to-expanding-them/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.climatechangenews.com/2025/05/13/trump-shifts-us-energy-funding-from-shutting-down-foreign-fossil-fuels-to-expanding-them/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1760529771440000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Ab2VYWWLDz9YgTe2DZw1u&quot;&gt;the new U.S. administration&lt;/a&gt; and is also supported by &lt;a id=&quot;m_-94292403662109932OWA4cc967fc-856a-09ed-35ba-e4ea0d7fc439&quot; href=&quot;https://energychamber.org/african-countries-must-oppose-measures-at-cop27-that-prevents-africa-from-making-full-use-of-its-fossil-fuels/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=https://energychamber.org/african-countries-must-oppose-measures-at-cop27-that-prevents-africa-from-making-full-use-of-its-fossil-fuels/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1760529771440000&amp;usg=AOvVaw06341tG2aUmJI7quypIpH4&quot;&gt;developing country experts&lt;/a&gt;. Yet, the reality remains that greenhouse gas emissions (GHG) from fossil fuels, and specifically the climate change they induce, can severely undermine &lt;a id=&quot;m_-94292403662109932OWA0516ca47-f12f-a125-14f7-320996cc281f&quot; href=&quot;https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/feature/2021/08/12/is-your-project-robust-to-the-impacts-of-climate-change-and-disasters&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/feature/2021/08/12/is-your-project-robust-to-the-impacts-of-climate-change-and-disasters&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1760529771440000&amp;usg=AOvVaw20ZLOX0N0qjK96w49f5zoA&quot;&gt;multilateral development bank projects&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a id=&quot;m_-94292403662109932OWA4ec5f867-f9b7-7459-5fd9-745172c93b5f&quot; href=&quot;https://www.usglc.org/blog/climate-change-and-the-developing-world-a-disproportionate-impact/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.usglc.org/blog/climate-change-and-the-developing-world-a-disproportionate-impact/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1760529771440000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0NP8g1Obu5GUBw8MAxVLsL&quot;&gt;overall developing country growth prospects&lt;/a&gt;.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/10/14/41323&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “World Bank and Other MDBs Need to Tackle Rich Country GHG Emissions to Support Development”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2025/10/Privatization_-629x419-1-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/10/14/41325</id><title>Global South Can Rebalance Climate Agenda in Belém, Says Gambian Negotiator</title><updated>2025-10-14T09:27:43-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/10/14/41325" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2025/10/Water-insecurity.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2025/10/Water-insecurity.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;NAIROBI, October 14 (IPS)  - The Gambia’s lead negotiator on mitigation believes that COP30 presents a unique opportunity to rebalance global climate leadership.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/10/14/41325&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Global South Can Rebalance Climate Agenda in Belém, Says Gambian Negotiator”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2025/10/Water-insecurity-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/10/14/41322</id><title>UNICEF Calls for Global Support to Protect Displaced and Starving Children in Haiti</title><updated>2025-10-14T06:21:02-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/10/14/41322" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2025/10/A-child-gazes-to_.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2025/10/A-child-gazes-to_.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
UNITED NATIONS, October 14 (IPS)  - New figures from the United Nations Children’s Fund (&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.unicef.org/press-releases/number-displaced-children-haiti-almost-doubles-one-year&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;UNICEF&lt;/a&gt;) show that displacement has surged significantly in Haiti, deepening existing security and humanitarian crises in a country where nearly 90 percent of the capital is controlled by armed gangs.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/10/14/41322&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “UNICEF Calls for Global Support to Protect Displaced and Starving Children in Haiti”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2025/10/A-child-gazes-to_-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/10/14/41321</id><title>From Algorithms to Accountability: What Global AI Governance Should Look Like</title><updated>2025-10-14T06:04:44-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/10/14/41321" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2025/10/ITU-Rowan-Farrell_.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2025/10/ITU-Rowan-Farrell_.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
ABUJA, Nigeria, October 14 (IPS)  - &lt;a href=&quot;https://hai.stanford.edu/assets/files/hai_ai_index_report_2025.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recent research&lt;/a&gt; from Stanford’s Institute for Human-Centered AI warns that bias in artificial intelligence remains deeply rooted even in models designed to avoid it and can worsen as models grow. From bias in hiring of men over women for leadership roles, to misclassification of darker-skinned individuals as criminals, the stakes are high.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/10/14/41321&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “From Algorithms to Accountability: What Global AI Governance Should Look Like”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2025/10/ITU-Rowan-Farrell_-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/10/14/41332</id><title>Israel restricts Gaza aid, saying Hamas must do more to return deceased hostages</title><updated>2025-10-14T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/10/14/41332" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/14-10-2025_UNICEF_Gaza-01.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/14-10-2025_UNICEF_Gaza-01.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Israel announced late on Tuesday that it will limit the flow of aid to Gaza, accusing Hamas of breaching the ceasefire agreement by returning only four of the bodies of deceased hostages so far.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/10/14/41332&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Israel restricts Gaza aid, saying Hamas must do more to return deceased hostages”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/14-10-2025_UNICEF_Gaza-01.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/10/14/41331</id><title>Humanitarians call for greater support amid immense needs</title><updated>2025-10-14T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/10/14/41331" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/29-09-2025-UNICEF-Bangladesh-05.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/29-09-2025-UNICEF-Bangladesh-05.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;With the end of the year fast approaching, humanitarians are urging donors to step up support for their operations which remain underfunded due to brutal cuts to aid budgets. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/10/14/41331&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Humanitarians call for greater support amid immense needs”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/29-09-2025-UNICEF-Bangladesh-05.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/10/14/41330</id><title>The ‘clean revolution is unstoppable’ but will it arrive too late?</title><updated>2025-10-14T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/10/14/41330" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/15-08-2025-UNDP-Bosnia-Herzegovina.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/15-08-2025-UNDP-Bosnia-Herzegovina.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A new report released on Tuesday warns the world is falling behind on its clean energy goals, prompting UN chief António Guterres to call once more for a ramped-up transition to a net zero global economy.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/10/14/41330&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “The ‘clean revolution is unstoppable’ but will it arrive too late?”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/15-08-2025-UNDP-Bosnia-Herzegovina.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/10/14/41329</id><title>UN envoy warns Libya’s transition at risk amid stalled political roadmap</title><updated>2025-10-14T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/10/14/41329" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/20-08-2024-UNICEF-Libya-02.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/20-08-2024-UNICEF-Libya-02.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The UN’s top envoy for Libya warned on Tuesday that the country’s long-delayed political transition will stay on hold unless rival institutions swiftly resolve differences over election laws and key appointments.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/10/14/41329&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “UN envoy warns Libya’s transition at risk amid stalled political roadmap”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/20-08-2024-UNICEF-Libya-02.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/10/14/41328</id><title>Ukraine: Top humanitarian strongly condemns Russian attack on UN aid convoy</title><updated>2025-10-14T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/10/14/41328" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/14-10-2025_Ukraine%20WHO.jpeg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/14-10-2025_Ukraine%20WHO.jpeg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Russian drones hit a “clearly marked” UN convoy on Tuesday which was bringing desperately needed aid to a war-torn frontline town in southern Ukraine. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/10/14/41328&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Ukraine: Top humanitarian strongly condemns Russian attack on UN aid convoy”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/14-10-2025_Ukraine%20WHO.jpeg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry></feed><!-- 0.0017s -->